    "summary": "I couldn't get five drawers into one hex base. Drawers only fit on the flat cut face of a half base, and a half base has just one cut face. I checked each shape: a full base took no drawers, a quarter base took none, and a half base took exactly one. So the build is one north-half hex base with one drawer on its cut face, and nothing else. I didn't add end caps or joint bolts (the usual finishing steps) because you asked for nothing else on the base. The check passed with no rule errors and no collisions between parts. If you want five drawers, you'd need five half bases, which means going past the single base you asked for.",
